     The ssiiggsseettmmaasskk() function sets the current signal mask to the specified
     _m_a_s_k.  Signals are blocked from delivery if the corresponding bit in _m_a_s_k
     is a 1.  The ssiiggbblloocckk() function adds the signals in the specified _m_a_s_k
     to the current signal mask, rather than overwriting it as ssiiggsseettmmaasskk()
     does.  The macro ssiiggmmaasskk() is provided to construct the mask for a given
     _s_i_g_n_u_m.

     The system quietly disallows SIGKILL or SIGSTOP to be blocked.

